## 2. Lebanese telecom numbers, Meta account model, and Kapso

### Recommended number and ownership pattern

Buy Alo King’s primary production number in the company’s legal name on a **corporate postpaid plan**. Alfa is the first carrier to document a substantive corporate checklist; touch is a valid alternative if it confirms a one-line or small-fleet route. Do not use a personal prepaid line as the sole production WhatsApp identity.

- **Alfa:** its Corporate Offer covers 5–20, 21–50, and 51+ line fleets and lists an authorized-person agreement, a recent commercial circular, stamped commercial register, Ministry of Finance registration certificate, company-name direct debit, and administrator/authorized-person IDs. Alfa’s general prepaid lifecycle is 10 days of validity followed by 12 days of retention, with progressive service degradation and expiry; accumulated validity is capped at 366 days. [13]
- **touch:** its Corporate Offer is publicly framed for organizations with more than five corporate postpaid lines and has 5–20, 21–50, and 51+ tiers. Its corporate M2M material lists a commercial register, signatories register, authorizations, and signed contract for data SIMs, but does not publish a complete voice-line dossier or a one-line exception. Corporate Sales is listed at **+961 3 792099 / seg@touch.com.lb**. [15] [16]
- **Ogero:** use for a fixed office line/PBX, not as the default mobile identity. Its business landline onboarding requires identity, premises/title or lease evidence, and commercial publication for institutions/companies. Ogero publishes an overdue sequence in which two unpaid bills can bar outgoing calls, three can bar incoming and outgoing calls, followed after a grace period by cancellation. [17]

Persist in Supabase: E.164 number, carrier legal owner, SIM custodian, billing account, bill/expiry status, Meta Business Portfolio ID, WAAC ID, Messaging/WABA ID, phone-number ID, Kapso project/customer ID, display-name status, two-step-verification state, and admin ownership. Alert on carrier billing, Meta status, display name, WABA/WAAC, and webhook failures.

### Meta’s 2026 account model and migration risk

Meta’s 2026 model separates a **WhatsApp Account (WAAC)**—one phone number/business identity—from a **Messaging account** for templates, billing, analytics, and webhooks. Existing WABA IDs continue as Messaging-account IDs during the staged rollout. General availability began **23 September 2026**, with rollout expected to reach all businesses by mid-October 2026. [18] [21]

New business portfolios initially have capacity for **two registered business phone numbers**; verification or a 2,000 messaging limit can automatically raise the cap to 20. Portfolio-level messaging limits are shared across numbers and are documented as 250 initially, then 2,000, 10,000, 100,000, and Unlimited through scaling/automatic scaling. [19] [20]

Meta’s current programmatic migration documentation says migration is **not supported on the new account model** when the destination WAAC does not already own the number. Disconnecting the current account does not make the number available; sharing the owning WAAC is the supported pattern. Do not remove a production number from its WABA/WAAC merely to experiment. Use a separate test number and inspect whether the account is legacy or new before migration. [22]

Kapso’s Bring Your Own SIM flow requires Alo King to control and verify the number, have it available for SMS/voice, and connect it through the Business Portfolio that owns it. Kapso-managed instant-setup numbers are not the appropriate substitute for a local, company-owned Lebanese number. [23] [24]

### Provider-confirmation items

- **Alfa:** Is one newly formed company-owned corporate postpaid line permitted? What are the exact documents, deposit/direct-debit requirements, billing suspension/reconnection stages, SIM replacement/delegation, owner-change, and post-cancellation reassignment rules?
- **touch:** Is a one-line exception available? What are the complete voice-line legal documents, minimum commitment, billing suspension/reconnection, owner-change, SIM delegation, and reassignment terms?
- **Ogero:** Can the proposed business line/PBX reliably receive Meta’s international voice-verification call? What are current activation, owner-change, overdue, reconnection, and cancellation fees?
- **Kapso:** For Alo King’s current account model, should the WAAC be shared rather than the number migrated? Confirm BYON ownership, number removal/reconnect consequences, WABA/WAAC IDs, webhook behavior, data processing, subprocessors, and support SLA.
- **Meta:** Confirm current portfolio capacity, WAAC/Messaging-account IDs, number ownership, display-name state, two-step verification, migration eligibility, and whether Alo King is in the legacy or new model.

