## 7. Vendor fields, uploaded dataset, and Google Places permissions

### Current dataset as an operational input

The uploaded vendor dataset contains **2,087 rows**, with **1,823 `phone_e164` values present**, **1,202 WhatsApp candidates**, **722 website/menu links**, **264 rows missing `phone_e164`**, **22 duplicate `phone_e164` values**, and **171 duplicate normalized names**. These are data-quality and outreach-planning statistics, not proof that a number is owned by a merchant, that WhatsApp contact is consented, or that a vendor is operational.

Before outreach, deduplicate by verified legal/business identity and normalized E.164 number, validate ownership/consent, and separate merchant-submitted fields from any Google-derived fields. Treat website/menu links as durable only where Alo King has independent rights to retain and use them.

### Verified Google rules and safe schema

- Place Details (New) requires an explicit field mask; requesting `*` is not the safe default. [62] [63]
- `place_id` may be stored indefinitely. Google recommends refreshing IDs older than **12 months** with an ID-only request; handle `NOT_FOUND` and `movedPlaceId`. [66]
- Google generally prohibits pre-fetching, caching, storing, exporting, indexing, extracting, or rehosting Google Maps Content, and explicitly prohibits bulk downloading places information or copying/saving business names, addresses, or reviews. [38] [67]
- Under the current non-EEA service-specific terms, only Places latitude/longitude has the explicit temporary-cache allowance of up to **30 consecutive calendar days**. Do not interpret that as permission to retain other Place fields for 30 days or longer. [39] [68]
- `regularOpeningHours` represents typical hours; `currentOpeningHours` covers today plus the next six days and includes special hours. Delivery and takeout booleans do not prove Alo King ordering acceptance, service-area coverage, or driver availability. [63] [64]
- Google’s documented Place fields do not include Instagram, WhatsApp/wa.me, Instagram-bio, or menu URLs. `websiteUri` is a business website, not a menu/social/WhatsApp field. Cuisine-adjacent types include Lebanese, Middle Eastern, Mediterranean, shawarma, falafel, halal, and restaurant. [63] [65]
- Request `languageCode` as `en` or `ar` as appropriate. `displayName` is localized and may fall back to the closest available language. [62] [71]
- When displaying Google-derived content without a Google map, provide the required Google Maps attribution/logo or prescribed text treatment and a Google Maps link where applicable. Do not combine Google Places content with a non-Google map. [38] [68]
- Google’s official material is inconsistent on the billing tier for `priceLevel` between the Place Details and Place Data Fields pages; recheck the live pricing matrix before launch rather than hard-coding rates. [62] [63]

### Recommended data model

Keep a small Google reference/read-through record:

- durable `google_place_id`, source timestamp, language, requested field mask, last lookup, and `moved_place_id`/`NOT_FOUND` state;
- no raw Google Place Details JSON as a durable vendor snapshot;
- temporary coordinates hard-deleted at 30 days if used;
- attribution and Google Maps link in any customer-facing display.

Keep durable Alo King/merchant records separately:

- legal and trading names in Arabic/English;
- merchant-submitted and verified Instagram URL, `wa.me`/ordering number, menu URL, website, cuisine taxonomy, price band, delivery/takeaway capability, service area, and ordering hours;
- source, consent/permission, verification actor, `verified_at`, `last_checked_at`, and expiry;
- Alo King visibility, onboarding, orderability, suspension, and service-level status—never conflated with Google `businessStatus`.

Use a user-triggered server-side Places lookup with the smallest field mask and requested language. Use Google as a cross-check at customer interaction when freshness matters; require merchant confirmation for operational ordering windows.

