## Implementation priorities

### P0 — launch gates

1. Appoint Lebanese counsel/tax adviser and request written BdL classification after Circular 777.
2. Confirm SARL status, contracts, principal/agent/MoR role, VAT position, invoice flow, refund/chargeback owner, CNSS/driver model, and municipal/food permits.
3. Send the provider question set below to Whish, OMT, Alfa, touch, Ogero, Kapso, Meta, and Google; do not treat marketing pages as technical approval.
4. Obtain written insurance endorsements and quotations for commercial delivery, cargo, cash, rider, third-party, own-bike, and high-risk-area exposure.
5. Archive Meta’s official 1 October 2026 USD rate card and reconcile the applicable Kapso/BSP markup and tax treatment.

### P1 — identity, ledger and controls

1. Buy and document the company-controlled postpaid number; create the Alo King Meta Business Portfolio/WAAC/Messaging account and Kapso BYON connection.
2. Build the provider adapter, immutable double-entry ledger, webhook verification, idempotency, refund/chargeback states, and USD/LBP separation.
3. Implement operational/marketing/call consent, STOP/block/withdrawal handling, and Arabic/English notices.
4. Clean the vendor dataset: de-duplicate 22 duplicate phone values and 171 duplicate normalized names, validate the 1,202 WhatsApp candidates, and resolve the 264 missing phone values without treating unverified records as outreach-ready.
5. Create the Google read-through schema, field-mask policy, 30-day coordinate deletion job, attribution components, and 12-month Place ID refresh workflow.

### P2 — bounded pilot

1. Pilot one Alo King merchant-of-record account, Whish first, with OMT as a separately approved comparison.
2. Start with prepaid diaspora baskets and a narrow merchant/zone set; allow COD only under the cash controls.
3. Run the courier pilot for two-to-four weeks; collect route, wait, deadhead, failure, cash, fuel, incident, and claim data.
4. Track card approval, manual review, delivery failure, substitutions, refunds, recipient OTP, chargebacks, Meta message cost, and provider settlement variance.

### P3 — scale only after evidence

1. Re-price courier zones from observed 50th/80th-percentile cost and risk data.
2. Add additional Messaging accounts or numbers only after capacity, billing, and account-model effects are confirmed.
3. Expand to recurring family baskets, custom lists, and occasion baskets before a broad marketplace.
4. Add vendor/driver payouts, automated reconciliation, and additional payment rails only after provider, regulator, legal, and insurance gates clear.

